# ── TestCase individuals: src/composition/tests/admission_notification.rs (CP10) ──

test:tc_max_admission_pushes_on_change a test:TestCase ;
    test:file test:File_admission_notification ;
    test:function "max_admission_pushes_lsp_max_admission_changed_when_the_verdict_actually_changes" ;
    test:assertionKind test:StateTransition ;
    test:asserts "forcing a real ERROR-severity diagnostic into the process-global registry, then calling the real ComposedServer::max_admission handler, causes exactly one real lspMax/admissionChanged notification (carrying the correct verdict payload) to arrive on a real Client/ClientSocket loopback pair, both for the forced transition and for reverting it back" ;
    test:provesReal "lspMax/admissionChanged is a real, end-to-end wired push notification reaching a real client when an admission verdict genuinely changes -- not just a Notification impl and a send-wrapper that nothing ever calls (the pre-CP10 dead-code state CP0's research found)" .

test:tc_max_admission_no_push_on_no_change a test:TestCase ;
    test:file test:File_admission_notification ;
    test:function "max_admission_does_not_push_when_the_verdict_is_unchanged" ;
    test:assertionKind test:NoTransition ;
    test:asserts "calling max_admission twice with no registry change in between yields the same verdict both times, and no second lspMax/admissionChanged notification arrives on the socket within a 50ms race window" ;
    test:provesReal "the admission-change push is real change-detection keyed on an actual verdict transition, not a blind notification sent on every poll" .

# ── TestCase individuals: crates/lsp-max-cli/tests/cp11_fitness_bridge.rs (CP11) ──

test:tc_diagnostic_content_survives_round_trip a test:TestCase ;
    test:file test:File_cp11_fitness_bridge ;
    test:function "diagnostic_content_survives_compositor_to_fitness_file_to_mcp_read" ;
    test:assertionKind test:FieldContent ;
    test:asserts "a synthetic diagnostic (distinctive URI, message, and ANDON-classified GGEN-TPL-001 code) deposited into a real DiagnosticBuffer, flushed through a real FlushCoordinator background task, appears -- by its real URI as a case_id, with a real non-UNKNOWN law_status -- in the JSON snapshot returned by lsp_max_cli::mcp_bridge::read_fitness_status_at, the exact function lsp-max-mcp's tool handlers call" ;
    test:provesReal "the existing LSP-to-MCP pull bridge (compositor deposit -> flush -> fitness-snapshot file -> mcp_bridge read function) is real and carries actual diagnostic content end-to-end, not just file presence -- previously evidenced only by scattered comments and manual reasoning, now a single automated Chicago-TDD proof" .
